      "summary": ": Tuesday 11th August Weather and snow- A mostly fine day in the forecast with light winds. We've had some temperature fluctuation over the past few days, so snow conditions are in a bit of a melt - freeze cycle; firm at first and expected to soften as the sun gets on it. Plenty of overnight grooming - hit some corduroy early while off piste softens up a bit. Event today - We're stoked to be hosting the Junior National Slalom Comp on Skite today - that run will be closed for the duration of the event.",
